Appeals are allowed in part;
2. Judgment and award dated 05th November, 2022 passed in MVCs No.564 of 2019 and 565 of 2019 by the Senior Civil Judge and Motor Accident Claims Tribunal-VI,
Kudligi sitting at Sandur, is modified by holding that the claimants in both the appeals are entitled for compensation of only Rs.15,000/- under the head Funeral Expenses in lieu of Rs.25,000/- awarded by the Tribunal.

The compensation awarded by the Tribunal under other heads remain unaltered;
3. Amount in deposit, if any, be transmitted to the Tribunal forthwith for onward disbursal to the claimants;
4. Draw modified decree accordingly;
- 17 - The Divisional Controller,Nekrtc vs Smt. G. Gangamma W/O Late Nagaraj Alias ... on 13 June, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/93877578/
8 NC: 2024:KHC-D:7965-DB 5. Registry to send the trial court records along with copy of this judgment to the concerned court forthwith.

